files.notes:
config  = { nose, fins, boost, engine, paint } (any can be missing)
options = { ghost: draw missing parts dashed, hl: part key to highlight, flame: show engine flames, face: robot peeking out, plainFlame: no <use> refs (for images) }
Drawing space: viewBox -38 -112 76 144, base of the rocket at y = 0.

config  = { cockpit, wings, thrusters, core, paint } (any can be missing)
options = { ghost: draw missing parts dashed, hl: part key to highlight, flame: engine flames, pilot: markup for a head in the cockpit }
Drawing space: facing right, centered on 0,0, viewBox -64 -42 128 84.

view = { w, h, T (pixels per tile), camX, camY, t (ms), dpr }
options = { theme, shadow: { x (screen fraction 0 to 1), k (size, 1 = normal), lantern: true | false } | null, whisper: true (rarely
            shows a tiny hidden message inside a glitch), glitch: false to turn glitches off }
Gentle on purpose: glitches happen at most about once a second, last a tenth of a second, and only shift a thin stripe.
Nothing flashes more than three times a second. With "reduce motion" turned on there are no glitches and nothing spins.

say:    { who: narrator | robot | dog | peng | rock | flame, x: text or (names) => text, face?: happy | surprised | think }
puzzle: { set: nimbus | glacia | meridian | corona, n: 0 to 2 }   question kinds come from makePlan() in state.js
fly:    { to: place name, leg: f1 to f5 (see LEGS in state.js) } or { vow: true } for the brave words

Question shape: { id, kind, q, a: [accepted answers; the first is the one shown], clue, clue2?, d (difficulty 1 easy, 2 medium, 3 hard), seq?, tiles?, eq?, len? }
Banks live in content/questions/*.js and register with addBank(name, kind, idPrefix, rows), rows = [id, d, question, answers, clue, clue2?].
Generators live in content/questions/*.js too: Kit.questions.gens.name = level => question.

Units are tiles and seconds. The ground's top is y = 0, and y goes up. The physics runs in fixed 1/120 s steps,
so a list of button presses (one per step) always replays exactly the same way.

Chunk format (see content/levels/runner-chunks.js): { id, min, max, len, w, tag, gaps: [[x0, x1]], o: [[kind, x, y, w, h]] }
  kinds: b block (x, y, w, h), s spike pointing up (x, y), v spike hanging down (x, y = its top), p bounce pad (x, y),
         S ship portal (x), C hero portal (x), x secret box (x, y). Ground is added under the chunk except in gaps.

generate({ chunks, level, speed, length, pieces, rng, secret }) -> { L, inputs, checks, endX, secret: { from, inputs } | null, frames }
  Picks chunks for the level, proves each one can be beaten, then places memory pieces along the winning path.

play(canvas, { gen, theme, drawBackground(ctx, view), drawHero(ctx, x, y, size, hero), onAttempt(n), onCrash(n),
              onCollect(obj), onMode(mode), onFinish(result), autopilot(), speedup(), tip })
  result = { attempts, crashes, pieces, piecesTotal, secret, usedCheckpoints, ms }

options = { width (tiles), start (tile x), speed (tiles per second), stops: [{ id, x, open }],
            draw(ctx, view, hero, bubble), onEnter(stop), onNear(stop or null), onTap(worldX, worldY, view) -> true if handled,
            onFirstMove(), onType(lastLetters) }
view = { w, h, T, camX, camY: 0, t, dpr, ground (pixel y of the floor) }; hero = { x, facing (1 right, -1 left), walking, near }
bubble = { text, until } for a speech bubble over the hero, set with say().

dig options:  { head, tip, words, shovelHtml, backHtml, onBack, onWord(i), onDone(stats) }
              tip = one short line telling the player what to do, shown above the dirt (there's no text box, so it isn't obvious)
line options: { text, onDone(stats, doneEl) }    doneEl is an empty .actions element for the Next button
stats = { hits, misses, ms, chars }
